<title>USA: Wetter weather moving into Europe - WSC.</title>
<headline>Wetter weather moving into Europe - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wetter weather is moving into areas of Western Europe where moisture is badly needed, including the UK, France, and Spain, independent forecaster Weather Services Corporation (WSC) said on Monday.</p>
<p>A frontal system is coming in off the Atlantic, and much cooler to colder air will move in behind it by midweek.</p>
<p>Southeast Europe will be fair and warm.</p>
</text>
